11124"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cce53189-83e8-5ab9-9abc-cb159f761f55" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049217}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193202} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193203} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526007} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526051} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526063} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526071}] :knowledge-point/title "Log-Likelihood Functions for Continuous Random Variables"} :step/id #uuid "d277bc8e-9565-50d6-8915-76af5cc26d62" :step/math-academy-id 42304 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193686}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193689 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193899 :tutorial/content "Recall that if $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed *continuous* random variables with probability density function $f(x; \\theta),$ then the likelihood function $L(\\theta)$ of a random sample $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(\\theta) = \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\\,\\theta)\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x;\\theta)$ is the probability density function of $X_i$ for $i=1,2,\\ldots, n,$ and $\\theta$ is an unknown parameter.\n\nSimilar to the case of discrete random variables, the **log-likelihood function** is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(L(\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{1};\\,\\theta )\\cdot f({x}_{2};\\,\\theta )⋯f({x}_{n};\\,\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{1};\\,\\theta ))+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{2};\\,\\theta ))+⋯+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{n};\\,\\theta )) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta )).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's get some practice at calculating log-likelihood functions for some continuous random variables." :tutorial/id #uuid "c0170775-4a1b-50a6-8f90-446fcc21a159" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7005 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4f38c06c-0588-54af-b61c-d056d9ae479e" :step/math-academy-id 42305 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193688}}] :activity/title "Log-Likelihood Functions for Continuous Probability Distributions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192934}]}
